.TH "CHARACTERDATA.REPLACEWITH" "3JS" "October 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CharacterData.replaceWith \- CharacterData: replaceWith() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]replaceWith()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] interface replaces this
\f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] in the children list of its parent with a set
of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects or strings.
Strings are inserted as equivalent \f[CR]Text\f[R] nodes.
Nothing happens if \f[CR]parentNode\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
replaceWith(param1)
replaceWith(param1, param2)
replaceWith(param1, param2, /* \&..., */ paramN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]param1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]paramN\f[R]
A set of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects or strings to insert.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]HierarchyRequestError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown when the node cannot be inserted at the specified point in the
hierarchy.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]p\f[R] id=\(dqmyText\(dq>Some text</\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] text = document.getElementById(\(dqmyText\(dq).firstChild;
\f[B]const\f[R] em = document.createElement(\(dqem\(dq);
em.textContent = \(dqItalic text\(dq;

text.replaceWith(em); \f[I]// Replace \(gaSome text\(ga by \(gaItalic text\(ga\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CharacterData.replaceData()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]DocumentType.replaceWith()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Element.replaceWith()\f[R]
